<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal- Most basis flat, some pricing.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal- Most basis flat, some pricing.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monday's sharp drop in CBOT soymeal futures spurred some pricing from end-users in spot markets, but most activity slowed as prices again worked their way higher early Tuesday, U.S. dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We saw active pricing yesterday with the board dropping the way it did,&quot; said a central Indiana dealer.</p>
<p>Monday, spot soymeal futures fell more than half the daily trading limit, but recovered a bit Tuesday. At 1006 CDT, July soymeal was up $1.70 at $299.70 per ton.</p>
<p>Other dealers said the market's current high prices have dampened buying enthusiam.</p>
<p>Livestock dealers are increasingly turing to less expensive feed options when they are available, soymeal merchants said.  </p>
